  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in New York are concentrated and smaller in FY2027 to date than in prior years. The state recorded $130M in obligations across 6,397 awards, with an average award size of $20.3K and year-over-year change down 98.9%. Fiscal-year totals from FY22 through FY27 show a sharp drop from $29.4B in FY22 to $11.3B in FY26 and then to $130M in FY27. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations, with $115M. A small group of vendors and industries account for most of the FY2027 to date spending, with SIEMENS HEALTHCARE DIAGNOSTICS INC. at $16.1M and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing at $21.2M. Readers should note that FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial; the raw numbers above are contract obligations for the period reported.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.9% year over year, from prior fiscal totals to $130M in FY2027 to date. The multi-year series shows FY22 at $29.4B, FY23 at $16.5B, FY24 at $15.1B, FY25 at $12.1B, and FY26 at $11.3B, before the FY27 to date figure of $130M. The number of awards in FY2027 to date is 6,397, with an average award size of $20.3K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying in FY2027 to date with $115M in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration at $8M and the Department of Defense at $4M. SIEMENS HEALTHCARE DIAGNOSTICS INC. is the top vendor at $16.1M, followed by DIRECT ENERGY BUSINESS LLC at $10.3M and ERNST & YOUNG LLP at $6.8M. Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing is the largest industry category at $21.2M, with Electric Power Distribution next at $14.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
